DELIVERED
Operator-only ctl identity status/unlock and Settings Account/Custody Unlock. The existing admitted door/window principal plus a private journal-validated device reference admits these two verbs while custody is held; public held status still hides the device ID. Native IO is bounded and off the worker/UI thread. Status/Check result is read-only even for a missing original operation; Unknown never automatically replays an interactive act. Each new explicit Unlock permits at most one interactive native access. A remaining second-item hold keeps Unlock available after Allowed.

The account/control pending envelope is published before native access with signature pending and an honest hold signer. Its chain position is immutable. When the expected legitimate device key returns, one appended completion binds the original op, real digest and stream position; the native outcome is retained, including Unknown. Pending inventory remains visible. No new principal or second operation ledger was added.

Native readers prefer <account>.dr1 and fall back only when it is absent, never after its refusal. Migration verifies the same key noninteractively before deleting the legacy item; restart cleanup never prompts. New login items and both signing recipes use the stable app/team designated requirement. An already-recorded custody tier never silently falls back. Public ACL metadata remains Unknown where the public API cannot prove the full ACL.

